```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
Historic Courthouse
310 W 19th Street
Cheyenne, WY 82001
3:30 PM
Commissioners Board Room
Saturday, December 6, 2025
SPECIAL MEETING TO FILL VACANCY IN HD 10
Roll Call/Call to Order
Chairman Gunnar Malm, Vice Chairman Troy
Thompson, Commissioner Linda Heath,
Commissioner Don Hollingshead, Commissioner
Ty Zwonitzer
Present:
Appointments
1.
Consideration of an appointment to fill the vacancy in House District
10 of Wyoming Legislature (WS 22-18-111(a)(iii)).
25 - 577
Resolution, Appointment
Attachments:
Chairman Malm explained the purpose of the meeting was to appoint a person to fill
the vacancy for Wyoming House District 10. He explained that each candidate would
be interviewed individually and the order of interview would be determined by a
manual drawing. He said candidates waiting to be interviewed would be sequestered
in another room and would surrender their cell phones. He stated that following the
interviews, the board would meet in executive session for deliberations, and the vote
would be done in public.
Candidates were invited to approach the dais and select a number for the order of
their interview. Sharon Fain was the first interviewee, Justin Fornstrom second, and
Ron Rabou third.
Each commissioner asked questions of the candidates. Topics included water and
natural resources, economic development, property tax reform, the state budget, their
vision for the state's role in supporting community colleges and ensuring resources to
meet evolving workforce needs, private property rights, and the candidate's
qualifications for representing House District 10.
The board went into executive session at 5:11 pm.
The board reconvened at 5:27 pm.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Zwonitzer, to appoint Justin Fornstrom to fill the vacant
House District 10 position. The motion carried by the following vote:
